`t/load.t` is a bare `use_ok('Alien::gettext')`. The whole contract of this tools-Alien is `Alien::gettext->bin_dir` plus the eleven `alien_bins` from `dist.ini:10`, and none of it is asserted - a build that installs no binaries at all passes.

Done when: a test puts `bin_dir` on `PATH` (an empty list on a system install, which is fine) and runs `msgfmt --version` and `xgettext --version` (e.g. `Test::Alien::run_ok`), asserting exit 0 and a version line.

